   "text": "I read the structure in four pieces and joined them, then worked out the cyclopentane stereo from the wedges.\n\n**Left to right**\n- **Indazole:** a 2H-indazole with a 1-methylcyclopropoxy group at C5. Its C3 is bonded to the pyrimidine.\n- **Pyrimidine:** C4 carries the indazole, C6 carries the piperidine nitrogen, and C2 and C5 are plain CH.\n- **Linker:** a piperidine whose 4-position bears an ether oxygen to cyclopentane C1. Cyclopentane C3 bears an ether oxygen to a second piperidine's 4-position. This second piperidine nitrogen is attached to the isoindolinone aryl ring.\n- **Isoindolinone:** the aryl carbon next to the piperidine-bearing carbon carries F. The CH2 is attached on the F side of the ring and the C=O on the other side. The lactam nitrogen is attached to a glutarimide (piperidine-2,6-dione) at C3.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nThe cyclopentane is 1,3-disubstituted. One C\u2013O bond is hashed and the other is wedged, so the two oxygens are trans. Assigning CIP priorities at each centre gives (S,S). In the SMILES below, both centres are written `@` in the form `O[C@H]5CC[C@H](O\u2026)C5`, which corresponds to that assignment. The glutarimide carbon is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo label.\n\nI checked that the ring closures are consistent and that the SMILES matches the drawing atom for atom.\n\nSMILES: CC1(CC1)Oc1ccc2n[nH]c(-c3cc(N4CCC(CC4)O[C@H]5CC[C@H](OC6CCN(CC6)c6ccc7C(=O)N(C8CCC(=O)NC8=O)Cc7c6F)C5)ncn3)c2c1"
